# Internal operational notes — fleet topology, host roles, operator paths.
# The WHOLE directory, not one file: naming a single file left the rest
# untracked-but-not-ignored, so a `git add -A` would put them straight into
# this public repository. That is exactly how legacy-amd-bringup.md, which
# names internal hosts, reached a public commit once already.
.review/

# Agent skills synced in from revytechinc/skills by its sync.sh.
# These are absolute symlinks into a developer home directory; this
# repository is public and they are not part of the source tree.
.claude/
